# UNA display images only

Never pass original uploads (`src_orig`, `orig`, raw storage files) into `app/ui/atoms/image` or `next/image`. This applies to **web and native**, including profile photos, covers, feeds, lists, lightbox, and messenger.

UNA transcodes first. NEO only further resizes/caches that **display** URL (`src`, else `medium` / `small` / `thumb`).

```javascript
import { pickUnaDisplaySrc, toUnaDisplayImageItem } from 'app/lib/image-helpers';

// ✅ spread UNA object — getImageSrc ignores src_orig
<Image {...image} alt="" view="cover" />

// ✅ flatten for carousel / attach rows
const slides = images.map(toUnaDisplayImageItem).filter(Boolean);

// ❌ original upload (breaks next/image cache and ships huge JPGs)
src: obj.src_orig || obj.src
<Image src={image.src_orig} />
```

Do not add a second `<img>` / `next/image` import. Native already hits `/_next/image` via `getNativeOptimizedImageUrl` — it does **not** need `src_orig`.
